# Mixr Rules

You are building Mixr, a SwiftUI iPhone DJ / Auto Remix app.

## Source of truth

- **Audio / Auto Remix behavior:** root `AGENTS.md` for pulse, tempo, gain, tests. Mix-window / join grammar is locked in the `dj-remix-planning` skill (wins on Xirex pivot, hook-replace, hard cut, diet SFX).
- **UI craft:** this file for visual tokens and layout. Do not invent a new visual language.
- **Stack gates:** SwiftUI / AVFoundation / Instruments for app code. Do not apply web Motion, Tailwind, or React EDT patterns to Swift files.

## Stack

- SwiftUI, iOS 18+
- MVVM
- Real audio, import, export, and Auto Remix are in scope when the task asks for them

## Design language

Apple Music meets Linear: premium dark mode, Apple-style glass, subtle blur, translucent panels, thin borders, soft shadows, restrained purple glow, high contrast text.

Avoid: neon gamer aesthetics, flat black panels, rainbow gradients, excessive glow, generic AI UI, skeuomorphic DJ controls.

## Colors

Background: #050816  
Background Secondary: #080B16  
Surface: #111827  
Elevated Surface: #171E2E  
Primary Purple: #7C3AED  
Secondary Purple: #8B5CF6  
Text Primary: #FFFFFF  
Text Secondary: #9CA3AF  
Divider: #2A3142  
Waveform Pink: #FF5FA2  
Waveform Purple: #8B5CF6  
Waveform Red: #EF4444  
Waveform Yellow: #EAB308  
Waveform Blue: #0EA5E9  

Mixr's purple brand is intentional. Global anti-purple "AI slop" guidance does not apply to these tokens.

## Typography

Apple system fonts. SF Pro Display for logo / section titles / top bar. SF Pro Text for song titles, metadata, buttons, controls.

Suggested scale: App title 24 bold · Section 15 semibold · Song 13 semibold · Body 12 · Metadata 10 medium.

## Layout

Landscape for iPhone; rotate prompt when vertical. Main screen keeps sidebar, playback controls, waveform timeline, solo/mute, tools drawer, AI Suggestions, and export visible. No tab bar. No navigation-stack chrome. No modal-heavy UI.

## Materials

Glass: translucent dark surfaces, subtle blur, thin light border, soft inner depth, restrained shadows. Prefer shared layout metrics over size-specific forks. UI chrome fixes must land in the shared path used by every breakpoint.

## Coding behavior

- Prefer small, reusable SwiftUI components.
- Modify only relevant files; no drive-by refactors.
- Do not add dependencies unless asked.
- For multi-step features: brief plan, then implement. Do not block on approval unless the user asks.
- For audio changes: follow `AGENTS.md` completion standard (tests, render, diagnostics, audition, evidence).
